      "text": [
        ": سَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ يَتَزَوَّجُ اَلْوَلَدَ اَلزِّنَى فَقَالَ \"لاَ بَأْسَ إِنَّمَا يُكْرَهُ مَخَافَةَ اَلْعَارِ وَ إِنَّمَا اَلْوَلَدُ لِلصُّلْبِ وَ إِنَّمَا اَلْمَرْأَةُ وِعَاءٌ، \" قَالَ قُلْتُ فَالرَّجُلُ يَشْتَرِي اَلْجَارِيَةَ اَلْوَلَدَ اَلزِّنَى فَيَطَؤُهَا قَالَ \"لاَ بَأْسَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4485 - Thalabah ibn Maymun narrated from Abdullah ibn Hilal, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdillah (as) about a man who marries a child born of fornication.\nHe (as) said: \"There is no harm in it. It is only disliked due to the fear of disgrace. Indeed, the child belongs to the father, and the woman is merely a vessel.\"\nI said: What about a man who buys a bondwoman born of fornication and has relations with her?\nHe (as) said: \"There is no harm in it.\""
        ]
      }
    },
